# Generated from: specs/394-resume-consumed-repaired-publication-dispatch-after-pane-split-failure/requirements.md

Feature: Resume consumed repaired-publication dispatch after pane split failure
  A one-time repaired-publication recovery remains consumed while its exact unfinished
  dispatch can resume once through parameter-free execute.

  @AC1 @SCN001
  Scenario: Pane split fails before first consumption
    Given bare run has re-proven an available repaired-publication recovery
    When standard pane allocation from the actual controller pane fails
    Then no archive, recovery record, checkpoint tuple, pending dispatch, or worker is created
    And no product or failure-evidence byte changes

  @AC2 @SCN002
  Scenario: Consumption persists an exact pending dispatch
    Given a standard implement pane was allocated successfully
    When repaired-publication recovery crosses archive and consumption
    Then one CAS reserves the original invocation and exact prepared dispatch without a run recovery
    And the next CAS creates exactly one matching run recovery and marks dispatch pending before agent start
    And same-invocation crash-gap resume creates only the absent tuple, never a duplicate or allowance

  @AC3 @SCN003
  Scenario: Grounded revision-fourteen state is discoverable
    Given revision 14 stopped at issue 108 implement with pane_split_failed
    And invocation 571f27fa-bc11-4778-9034-b1b992e85638 is consumed with exact immutable archive proof
    And the owner is incomplete, workers are empty, no matching pane or agent exists, and product state is clean
    When parameter-free recovery discovery runs
    Then it returns consumed-dispatch-available for that same invocation
    And it does not offer ordinary loop recovery

  @AC4 @SCN004
  Scenario: Pending dispatch resumes the same invocation
    Given discovery offers one exact consumed dispatch
    When the next parameter-free bare run re-proves it under lease
    Then it allocates from actual controller geometry and starts only s108-implement
    And it does not consume, archive, or append recovery state again

  @AC4 @SCN005
  Scenario: Started dispatch cannot be offered twice
    Given same-invocation resumption has durably recorded standard worker start ownership
    When discovery repeats before or after prompt activation
    Then consumed dispatch is unavailable
    And no duplicate worker or invocation is created
    And validated implement completion clears only ephemeral pending dispatch before next-step or terminal persistence
    And immutable safe-recovery and run-recovery evidence remains

  @AC5 @SCN006
  Scenario Outline: Crash boundaries retain deterministic authority
    Given repaired-publication dispatch reaches <boundary>
    When controller execution stops
    Then durable state identifies either unconsumed recovery or the same pending invocation
    And cleanup closes only a proven-owned unused pane

    Examples:
      | boundary |
      | split before consumption |
      | pending persistence before start |
      | agent start failure after consumption |
      | successful start before prompt activation |

  @AC6 @SCN007
  Scenario Outline: Unsafe consumed dispatches stay blocked
    Given an otherwise exact consumed-dispatch fixture with <defect>
    When discovery or bare run evaluates resumption
    Then consumed dispatch remains unavailable
    And no run, recovery, handoff, archive, task, product, or workflow-evidence byte changes

    Examples:
      | defect |
      | non-pane failure |
      | missing or mutated archive |
      | changed run or head |
      | changed branch or owner |
      | changed handoff or task |
      | product or worktree drift |
      | complete owner |
      | existing worker, pane, or agent |
      | wrong invocation |
      | duplicate resume |
      | controller lock |
      | explicit selector |

  @AC7 @SCN008
  Scenario: Existing recoveries and generated surfaces remain stable
    Given existing repaired-publication and safe-recovery fixtures plus public workflow surfaces
    When focused, full, command-sync, plugin, current-spec, inventory, contribution, version, and diff checks run
    Then only exact same-invocation consumed-dispatch resumption changes behavior
    And every existing recovery class and one-time consumption rule remains unchanged
